 ### Slab Extrusion (Staircase Representation)
-A variant where slice data is thresholded and extruded in the axial direction by the slice-to-slice distance. These slabs are stacked and viewed using simple geometric routines to produce a staircase-like representation [S2, unofficial]. It is one of the first schemes used to view reconstructed contours [S2, unofficial].
