 ## Operating characteristics
-**Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of voxels, assuming constant-time face generation and culling. With an octree, traversal is proportional to the number of occupied leaf nodes [S3, unofficial].
-**Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for the binary array. $O(M)$ for the output mesh, where $M$ is the number of visible faces ($M \le 6N$). Octree storage reduces memory for sparse data [S3, unofficial].
